Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a use-after-free regression in the xHCI driver when the `Clear_TT_Buffer` work was scheduled. This occurred because the USB core was freeing and reallocating a new device for enumeration while the xHCI driver was still processing the clearing of the TT buffer. If the endpoint was disabled before the `hub_tt_work` finished, it would lead to dereferencing already freed pointers, resulting in undefined behavior.

