The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
xhci->devs[udev->slot_id];
ep->ep_state & EP_CLEARING_TT;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the xHCI driver attempts to access the `devs` array using a potentially freed `udev->slot_id`, and checks the state of the endpoint with `ep->ep_state & EP_CLEARING_TT` without ensuring that the `hub_tt_work` has completed. If the USB core has already freed and reallocated the device while the `Clear_TT_Buffer` work is still in progress, this leads to dereferencing already freed pointers, resulting in undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ep->ep_state & EP_CLEARING_TT) {
    schedule_timeout_uninterruptible(1);
    goto rescan;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that the xHCI driver waits for the `hub_tt_work` to finish clearing the hub TT before proceeding to disable the endpoint. By checking if the endpoint is in the `EP_CLEARING_TT` state and rescheduling if it is, the code prevents the use-after-free condition by ensuring that the endpoint is not disabled until it is safe to do so.

